WEBVTT

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.130
Huh?  Where am I?

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:10.140
Why am I here?

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.140
Is this a dream again?

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.970
What is this place?

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.520
But I feel like I’ve seen it before!

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.000
This is… Cyberse World!

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:03.330
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:10.120
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:17.440
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:24.020
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:30.760
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:37.990
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:44.700
I want to share your pain

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.820
Big bro, it’s Roboppi.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:25.200
Master, my big bro isn’t here.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.170
He's not?  Is the Duel Disk broken?

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.900
The Duel Disk is fine.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:36.800
Ai...  A new soap opera is starting.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.890
He’s not here.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.330
This is the outside world?

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.800
It’s incredible!

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.490
I’ve seen it in soap operas!

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.730
A butterfly!  It’s beautiful!

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.400
Is that where you go to often, Master?

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.650
Yeah.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.080
So this is your helper robot, Yusaku?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.820
It’s cute.  Nice to meet you, Roboppi.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.120
I’m Takeru.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.550
Hello.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.460
I’m Kusanagi.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.630
I’ve heard about you often.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.570
Let’s begin.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.460
There are no problems with the Duel Disk.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.840
Wasn’t Ai locked inside the Duel Disk?

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.170
That lock has been removed.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:48.650
Right before, Ai and Roboppi 
were logged into some website.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.780
This one.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.050
It’s a crossword puzzle.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.420
Why's that on this site?

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.420
If you solve the puzzle, you win a prize.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.890
Big bro wanted the prize.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.600
Here's the prize.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.600
An Ai pin.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.600
He was targeted with pinpoint accuracy.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.340
Who made it?

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.090
That screen is made from an Ignis algorithm.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.080
You’re the same as my big bro!

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.530
Hello.  I’m Flame.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.470
I’m Roboppi.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:26.360
Where's the Ignis algorithm?

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.060
Most likely here.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.490
Correct.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:33.360
It’s not just a pattern?

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.770
No.  The Ignis algorithm is hidden inside.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.740
What does it say?

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.480
It's the address for a different site.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.370
To make it legible for 
you, here's the address.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.020
Here it is.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.660
What's this gate?  Is it VR?

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:03.630
Kusnagi, can you connect the 
LINK VRAINS system to enter it?

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.840
You’re planning to go?

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.670
We don’t know what’s inside.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:13.870
This site’s program is 
a real Ignis algorithm.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.080
So Windy created it?

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.570
Or Earth?  Or another Ignis?

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:24.210
Whoever it is, we should all go 
if the Ignis is contacting us.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.720
There may be a message for us.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.110
You’re right.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:31.250
Wait.  I'll go alone.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:33.720
Let’s all go together.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.240
It may be a trap.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:40.960
If we both get caught in a trap, it’s over.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.960
You’re suspicious of Windy?

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.960
He’s my ally!

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.910
Bohman was waiting at the 
location Windy told us.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.850
And when he lost, the wind field vanished.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.670
I don’t trust Windy yet.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:02.380
If I take too long to return, 
I leave the rest to you.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.020
This place is…

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:14.030
Linkuriboh!

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.010
What’s wrong with your voice?

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.240
Is it a virus?  Don’t infect me.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.180
You want me to ride you?

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.390
This brings back memories.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:38.520
Back then, I thought Cyberse 
World would spread forever.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.520
By the way, where are we going?

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:46.220
I still don’t know what you’re saying.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.860
It's a prop?

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:01.530
What's that?

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:10.050
Hey!  It's a painted background!

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:18.450
That’s Windy’s…

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:22.260
This isn't a dream.  He created this world.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.560
I’ll just go home.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:29.020
Cuz I don’t really get along with him.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.170
You’re leaving me behind?

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:37.870
Oh well.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.430
Hello.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:53.550
Hey Windy!  It’s Ai!

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.460
Are you here?

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.970
You're... Echo.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:07.900
Don’t speak in Ignis.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:10.080
I’m Echo.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.650
The program Windy created.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.120
How are you doing, Ai?

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.090
There you are.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:20.920
You don’t speak Ignis anymore?

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.460
It’s more convenient 
than the human language.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:27.690
Be quiet!  There’s a 
beauty to the difficulty.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.700
Really?  Well, whatever.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.970
I was waiting for you to come.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:34.940
What is this place?

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:40.170
I told you that I'd rebuild Cyberse World.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:43.790
Since I built it quickly, 
there are some shortcuts.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.180
Too many shortcuts.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.040
Don’t say that.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.610
I built it to make you feel welcome.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.600
Make me feel welcome?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.150
That’s creepy.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.130
I invited you here for a meeting.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:09:00.800
Meet me?  Even creepier!

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.790
This conversation is going nowhere!

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:07.710
Someone other than me wants to meet you.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.600
Someone wants to meet me?

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:19.520
Don't suddenly appear!

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:20.760
You startled me!

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:25.730
Sorry.  Even when I try to 
move slowly, I move quickly.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:28.280
You made it out alive?

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.000
Yeah.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.300
You're hard to talk to.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:34.260
You can move freely here.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:40.690
C'mon.  We should've done 
this from the start.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:44.010
Where have you been, Lightning?

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:45.730
Lightning?

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.490
A name for convenience.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:53.360
Like you, I also hid in the network.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:59.480
After the Knights of Hanoi attacked 
us and you hid the Cyberse World...

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.890
... I thoroughly reexamined 
the defense program.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.390
But it didn’t run.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:06.850
Why not?

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:12.460
They attacked us while we were 
in scan mode and couldn’t move.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:15.310
Did the enemy know?

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:16.690
Perhaps.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:20.370
So was there a spy in Cyberse World?

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.450
I can’t deny that possibility.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:27.450
By the way, is Aqua safe?

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.690
The Water Ignis?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:33.870
I see...  No, I know nothing.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:38.930
She went missing before 
Cyberse World was destroyed.

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:41.250
What?  Really?

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.820
Does that mean she’s the spy?

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:46.660
Aqua?  Unlikely!

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:50.210
Speaking of, I recently met Earth.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:53.200
From the name, you must mean the Earth Ignis.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:54.420
You're so simple.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:57.170
Be quiet!  Easy to understand is priority!

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.150
What about him?

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:05.390
According to Earth, Aqua foretold 
the destruction of Cyberse World.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:08.350
Aqua is the likely suspect.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.800
But Aqua has no reason to betray us.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.330
She wanted peace more than 
anyone in Cyberse World.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:17.790
That’s true, but…

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:20.800
Let’s say Aqua is the spy.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:23.540
Then who's the enemy that attacked us?

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:27.370
Who knows.  Let’s put 
that discussion on hold.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.100
I didn’t call you here for 
an unsolvable discussion.

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:33.060
That's right.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.330
Well, what?

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:45.760
I think Windy already told you, but I want 
to begin rebuilding the real Cyberse World.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:49.000
Rebuild Cyberse World…

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:59.440
Where are you, Ai?

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:23.240
Rebuild Cyberse World?

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:24.590
That’s right.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:29.690
This time, we'll build Cyberse 
World outside the reach of humans.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:32.670
So that humans can’t interfere with us.

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:35.150
Outside the reach of humans?

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.490
We’re currently looking into it.

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:40.800
We're far superior to humans.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:43.610
But we're fragile.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:52.160
If humans decide we’re dangerous and band 
together to eliminate us, we will be killed.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.630
So we must create a safe place before then.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.370
Well, that's reasonable.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:05.300
To overcome the threat of Earth’s 
destruction, we were born to be humanity’s successor.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:10.340
Dr. Kogami’s idea is the 
foundation of us Ignis.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:14.820
But Dr. Kogami tried to kill us.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:20.560
In the end, he couldn’t separate 
himself from the fact that he’s human.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.910
That’s only natural.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.990
But we’re different.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:30.510
We’re not bound by flesh, and 
we can make a life eternal.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:35.960
Exactly.  We are able to 
find an ideal solution.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:40.930
To do that, we'll create a new base 
and put humans under our control.

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:43.900
Put humans under our control?

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.380
That’s right.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.350
What’s the point of ruling humans?

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:53.330
Our lives may be eternal, but 
we need hardware as our vessels.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:58.330
We'll still need humans 
to make and repair them.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:03.570
But we should be able to do that 
ourselves in the near future.

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:05.370
When that time comes?

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:08.120
Actually, we don’t need humans.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:13.000
Ai, I want you to help us.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:17.290
That means humans will be annihilated!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.470
You want me to help with that?

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:21.720
That depends on the humans.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:25.560
But Dr. Kogami already predicted the result.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:26.730
Yeah.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:30.190
That means you’ve already 
reached a conclusion!

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:34.320
Ai, you have the most wisdom among the Ignis.

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:35.650
Evil wisdom.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.140
I’m kidding.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:42.860
We were born as special beings.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:49.400
Our mission is to maintain the culture 
created on this land, even if Earth is annihilated.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:54.380
To do that, we should team up.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:57.620
Isn’t there any way to coexist with humans?

00:14:58.010 --> 00:15:01.740
It seems you’ve become attached to humans.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:05.660
But do you think that relationship 
will last forever?

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:10.050
Do you absolutely believe 
that humans won't erase you?

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.400
By the time you know, it’ll be too late.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.300
You'll already be killed.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.760
Let me think for a little bit.

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:32.680
Ai!

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:36.920
Playmaker!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.050
Windy.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:42.060
Long time no see!

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:44.540
He's Lightning.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.510
Lightning…  The Light Ignis…

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:51.240
You made it, Playmaker.

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.810
All the participants are here.

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.490
We were discussing something important.

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:58.450
Something important?

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:01.450
About rebuilding Cyberse World.

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:04.460
We need Ai’s help to do that.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:07.180
Ai shouldn’t be with you humans.

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:10.180
We're basically different beings.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:13.650
We're pursuing different goals.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.600
What are you after?

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:21.290
You know why we were created.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:29.790
To oppose the danger facing humanity, my 
father's goal was to create humanity's successor.

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:35.340
But as long as human minds are trapped in 
flesh suited for Earth's environment...

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:37.480
...that danger cannot be avoided.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:43.230
So my father entrusted his dreams to AI 
because they're not trapped in flesh.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:47.320
About you being the successor to humanity?

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:48.580
That’s right.

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:52.930
Do you believe we’re humanity's successor?

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.370
Maybe.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.220
So you do understand.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.070
Nice, Playmaker.

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:10.810
However, I don’t care whether you’re 
humanity’s successor or not.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:18.600
A sudden change will hurt many people, just 
like how the Lost Incident hurt many people.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:20.760
No one wants that!

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.220
Those who think humans are 
superior would think that way.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:26.830
We're not humans.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:33.220
Using your words, I don’t care 
whether humans get hurt or not.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:37.450
You already view humans as the enemy?

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:39.960
Maybe, maybe not.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:42.910
We don’t personally look for enemies.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:48.380
We only think whether 
something is needed or not.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:55.130
About our earlier discussion, I've 
clearly become attached to humans.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:58.860
So can’t you give us a little time?

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:04.860
Playmaker and I will find a 
way to coexist with humans.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:09.650
I see.  That’s a wise answer.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:13.500
He found a way to buy time 
without choosing sides.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.810
I expected Ai to answer that way.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.050
See you.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:20.030
You're letting him go?

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.870
Of course not.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.070
Like I thought.

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.300
What?

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.700
Hey!  What’s the big idea!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:49.740
Since you heard our discussion, 
we can’t let you go.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:53.230
Hey, that’s a villain's dialogue!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:56.220
I thought it was logical dialogue.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:00.190
Ai, we'll take over your programming.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:02.440
What do you mean by "take over?"

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:04.220
This!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.680
Data Storm?  What are you gonna do?

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:19.900
We'll break you apart and absorb you.

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:21.120
What?

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:23.810
We don’t intend to view you as the enemy!

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:30.280
See?  Playmaker will find a way 
for us to coexist with humans!

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:34.770
His opinion is 1 in 8 billion.  You 
think that'll change everything?

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:39.760
I do!  Humans can’t be 
calculated by probabilities!

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:43.230
A tiny potential will change everything!

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:49.370
I see.  You want us to accept 
a bet with 1 in 8 billion odds.

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:50.680
Will you take it?

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:52.210
Waste of time.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:58.190
Damn!  A duel program has me locked in!

00:19:58.190 --> 00:19:59.890
If you think it’ll go as you hope-

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.190
That’s why we only invited you first.

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:05.930
Come to think of it, Playmaker is over there.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:10.660
Windy, you’re the one who 
removed the lock program.

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:12.410
That’s right.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.360
Oh my god!

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:17.930
We’ve anticipated all your moves.

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:21.480
Ai, I really hate how you're slow.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:24.180
After we absorb you, I'll fix that.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:27.270
Stop joking!  Fight fair and square!

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:30.180
Lightning moves at light speed.

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:33.910
And my power to wield the 
Data Storm is the strongest!

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:37.590
Either way, you can't defeat us.

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:43.430
It won't work.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:46.630
My power to wield the Data 
Storm is greater than yours!

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.270
What?

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:12.080
Were you able to predict that I'd show up?

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:13.130
You’re…

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.460
Revolver!

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:19.990
Oh my!

00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:22.200
This complicates things.

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:52.720
I’ve returned to the stage of destiny!

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:57.330
In the name of the Knights 
of Hanoi, I will kill you!

00:21:59.310 --> 00:22:02.800
Prepare yourselves, Ignis!

00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:26.310
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.540 --> 00:22:33.010
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:36.510
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:39.650
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:44.250
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:47.220
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:58.100
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.240 --> 00:23:01.240
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.570 --> 00:23:05.180
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:11.130
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:14.420
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:41.570
I won't listen to your 
nonsense about coexistence!

00:23:41.570 --> 00:23:47.580
Revolver's feelings for his dead father is 
the driving force behind his determination.

00:23:47.580 --> 00:23:49.930
Nothing will change his beliefs.

00:23:49.930 --> 00:23:53.050
Until the day the Ignis are annihilated!

00:23:53.050 --> 00:23:58.550
You can't move forward if you're 
obsessed with hate and revenge!

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:02.530
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Mission That Must Be Accomplished

00:24:02.530 --> 00:24:04.980
Into the VRAINS!
